//     4 trust region, 5 CG, 6 quasi-Newton, 7 large-scale, 9 derivative-free, 10 least squares,
//     12 constrained theory, 13 simplex, 14 LP interior point, 15–18 constrained algorithms,
//     penalty/augmented Lagrangian, SQP).
//   - Stanford EE364a (Boyd) lecture/supplement page: https://web.stanford.edu/class/ee364a/lectures.html
//   - Wikipedia, List of numerical analysis topics (optimization section):
//     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_numerical_analysis_topics
// Gaps filled after comparison: Helly and Carathéodory, subgradients, Klee–Minty, Bland's rule, dual
//   simplex, KKT failure without constraint qualification, Maratos effect, filters, Karmarkar,
//   ellipsoid method, Löwner–John ellipsoids, lasso/TV denoising, SVMs.
// Momentum/Nesterov acceleration, SGD, proximal gradient and ADMM are not developed in either
//   reference; they are included as essential bridges to `ml`/`deep` and cited at chapter level.
// Deliberate omissions: integer programming and branch-and-bound (belongs to `algo`), dynamic
//   programming and optimal control (in `ctrl`), calculus of variations (in `mech`/`pde`),
//   compressed sensing (in `sig`), metaheuristics such as simulated annealing and genetic algorithms.
