      n: 5,
      title: 'Lagrange duality and the KKT conditions',
      summary: String.raw`Attaching prices to constraints gives the Lagrangian, and minimizing it over the variables gives a dual function that bounds the optimal value from below — weak duality, always. For convex problems with a strictly feasible point the bound is tight (Slater), and the optimal primal–dual pairs are characterized by the KKT conditions, including complementary slackness. Multipliers measure the sensitivity of the optimum to constraint changes, and theorems of alternatives such as Farkas’ lemma are duality in its purest form.`,
